GARDEN
VERSION HISTORY THROUGH v15.10
Plain UTF-8 text
History-only artifact
Updated: 2026-09-19

ROLE

This file records major design lineage.

It is NOT one of the three current controlling design sources.
An older release cannot override the current Book, Technical Design or Catalogue.
Historical labels are retained to explain where present structures came from.

EARLY / PRE-v10 LINEAGE

Garden began as a broad multi-part architecture for human-centered AI, knowledge, safety, governance, infrastructure,
real-world systems and long-run evolution. Early versions used a more fixed module/component framing.

The early lineage established several ideas that remained important:
    typed meaning rather than loose prompts;
    explicit safety/authority boundaries;
    human rights;
    proof/checking before consequential execution;
    traceable state change;
    knowledge/research/evolution loops;
    real-world physical and infrastructure integration.

v10.x — CONSOLIDATION OF THE LARGE DESIGN

2026-08-11 — v10.25 lineage
    A complete-design baseline existed with a simplified core-object framing and the large module architecture.
    Subsequent work expanded/reconciled the semantic object model.

2026-08-12 — v10.28 lineage
    Seven-theory and broad architecture work was consolidated.
    The Evolution process included proposal, anti-nonsense triage, applicability discovery, impact analysis, formal
    verification, implementation/rollback, validation, commit and recursive coverage checks.

v10.3x / vFINAL lineage
    Human sovereignty, personal transformation/consent, physical safety, rights and long-run design consolidation were
    expanded.
    Historical module numbering remained important for compatibility.

2026-08-20 to 2026-08-21 — self-explaining / human-centered rebuilds
    The design was reorganized for readability and more explicit ownership.
    Rights definitions, registry ownership, proof obligations, capability/domain owners, explanation, privacy,
    infrastructure and research structures were progressively normalized.
    Human Flourishing and the Absolute Human-Centric Principle were restored as active rights; later numbering settled
    them at RIGHT-024 and RIGHT-025, with RIGHT-026 RESERVED and RIGHT-027 ON_HOLD.

v11 / v12 / v13 LINEAGE

The design moved away from treating the old 50 modules as a permanently fixed ontology.

Key direction:
    preserve historical module meaning;
    move to typed architecture-object ownership;
    keep old numeric labels as compatibility aliases;
    centralize registries and stable IDs;
    reduce duplicate definitions.

v13.5 retained a verified old-50-module coverage map with all 50 historical names mapped to current owners.

v14 LINEAGE — FOUR/FIVE-FILE CANONICAL ORGANIZATION AND HARDENING

2026-08-23 — v14 baseline
    A four-file canonical baseline was established:
        Human
        System Flow
        Technical
        Annexures

2026-08-24 — v14.1 / v14.2 / v14.3 / v14.4 lineage
    Readability, references, assurance, standards and engineering-design integration progressed.
    GSL grammar/typing, rights ordering, registry centralization and cross-document ownership were tightened.

2026-08-25 — v14.5
    Canonical successor with retention checks, header normalization, assurance hardening and engineering-design
    integration.

2026-08-25 — v14.6
    Critical continuity phase and receipt structures strengthened.

2026-08-25 — v14.7
    AGI/cognitive hardening normalized.

2026-08-26 — v14.8 / v14.8.1 / v14.8.3
    Repaired and then split into five source files:
        Human
        System
        Technical
        Annexure
        Theories

    Documentation cleanup and theory ownership improved.

2026-08-27 — v14.8.4 / v14.8.5
    CASI and adapter hardening integrated.
    Engine.Reason replaced older orchestration wording in relevant cognitive paths.
    World-model and physical-cognitive boundary work was expanded.

Major theory versions in this lineage:
    SRT 1.0
    VSM 2.0
    RPM 2.0
    PPM 2.0
    TFT 1.1
    FET 1.0
    SCT 1.0

v15 LINEAGE — RECURSIVE QUALIFICATION, CAUSAL LEVERAGE AND CLEANER OWNERSHIP

2026-09-11 — v15.0 / v15.1 / v15.2 lineage
    Successor work integrated recursive qualification and cognitive implementation ideas.

2026-09-11 — CPI v1.0 then CPI v1.1 candidate
    Cognitive Implementation & Recursive Qualification was refined.

2026-09-12 — v15.3
    Five-file successor preserving earlier v15.2 material while adding cross-layer hardening and CPI reconciliation.

2026-09-12 — v15.4
    Generalized Causal Leverage (GCL) and formal algebra work were admitted into the design line.
    Whole-corpus audit found stale release banners, GCL underspecification, missing IDs and duplicate foundational
    registrations.

2026-09-12 — v15.5
    The then-current five-file baseline repaired:
        stale release banners;
        GCL executable ratio/authority-reduction semantics;
        SchemaID dictionary updates;
        duplicate registrations through explicit alias/equivalence treatment.
    GSL v45.1 and the overall topology were retained.

2026-09-13 to 2026-09-16 — v15.6 / v15.7 candidate work
    Multiple gap-closure and hardening changes were developed:
        R0 SanityGate separated from recursive Reason modes;
        rights-view normalization;
        provenance-class/redaction-vs-absence distinction;
        authority/effect typing;
        human-effect and justice/reputation hardening;
        event-driven routing/context work;
        cognitive qualification and closure amendments.

    Some repo candidates remained noncanonical even when their design content was later carried forward.

2026-09-17 — v15.8
    Consolidation target for scattered v15.6/v15.7 work.
    The source was frozen for the v15.9 documentation rewrite after review.

2026-09-18 — v15.9
    Five-file documentation rewrite:
        Human
        System
        Technical
        Theories
        Annexure

    Main goals:
        one owner per semantic fact;
        reduce duplicated normative text;
        reorganize around concepts/owners instead of upgrade chronology;
        distinguish normative material from explanation;
        preserve CURRENT/CANDIDATE/DEFERRED/RESEARCH states;
        preserve specification != implementation != validation != certification;
        repair references and duplicated wording;
        keep traceability without making history the current source.

    RCI was normalized as a current-reading composition over existing owners, not a new Engine or authority root.
    Protected consequential self-change retained independence and verification requirements.

    Release status remained a working candidate unless separately admitted.

v15.10 — THREE-ARTIFACT SEMANTIC REPACKAGING

2026-09-18 to 2026-09-19

Goal:
    make the design substantially easier for both humans and machines to understand while preserving the complete
    v15.9/v15.x meaning.

The source model was reduced from five document roles to three semantic artifacts:

    Book
        ordinary-language explanation.

    Technical Core
        deterministic structure, typed mappings, Design Forms, validation/expansion and build rules.

    Catalogue
        exhaustive specific material: rules, IDs, rights, theories, equations, algorithms, profiles, exceptions,
        mappings and historical crosswalks.

Key v15.10 abstraction:
    seven Design Forms:
        CONSTRUCT
        CONTRACT
        STATE
        RELATION
        PROCESS
        RULE
        PROJECTION

Theory and Algebra became specializations/compositions rather than extra Design Forms.
Receipt was normalized as a Construct.
Schema was interpreted as structural Projection plus applicable admissibility/type rules/contracts.

The v15.10 design also normalized named deployment architectures as parameterized profiles/presets rather than new
authority roots.

Deterministic expansion:
    G0 -> F(G0) -> F^2(G0) -> ... -> G*

Unique equations, algorithms, timings, assumptions, fallbacks and profile meaning remained source seeds rather than being
left for a model to invent.

