v15.10 TEXT-ONLY REPRESENTATION CORRECTION

2026-09-19

The source-packaging rule was changed without intending a semantic redesign:

    all canonical Garden sources must be ordinary directly readable UTF-8 text;
    no gzip/zip/database/binary object is required;
    no external or historical file may supply missing current semantics;
    current semantic facts should have one controlling occurrence;
    predecessor whole-file embedding is not required merely for byte reconstruction;
    required old-ID/current-ID and migration mappings remain;
    history is separate from current design;
    generated graphs/indexes/caches are derivative.

The requested final user-facing layout is now:

    GARDEN_BOOK_v15.10.txt
    GARDEN_TECHNICAL_v15.10.txt
    GARDEN_CATALOGUE_v15.10.txt
    GARDEN_VERSION_HISTORY_v15.10.txt

Only the first three are current design sources.
The fourth is lineage/history and cannot override them.

CURRENT STATUS

Garden v15.10 remains a WORKING CANDIDATE unless admitted through the applicable Garden governance/admission path.

This history file records lineage; it does not certify implementation, safety, empirical performance or external
deployment.


2026-09-20 — v15.10 text-retention closure candidate
    A direct semantic-retention audit compared the compact Book + Technical + Catalogue against the frozen v15.9
    CurrentReadingMap, UpgradeTraceabilityTable and reviewed current anchors.
    Broad architecture/rights/theory retention was already present.
    Compact-source repair restored reviewed unique obligations that had become implicit or absent in the first text-only
    draft, including HRAP/protected reporting, CSI/SMCD/CAD/OAC/CTSN/PAI, CausalClosureReceipt, typed credential status,
    justice expiry/retry handling and their retained conformance obligations.
    The repair keeps review packet IDs/history non-controlling and does not re-embed predecessor bulk text.
    No new canonical authority, production certification, executable certification or independent semantic admission is
    created by this representation repair.


2026-09-20 — standalone no-loss current-source closure candidate
    The compact text design was upgraded from broad-marker retention to literal standalone retention. The current
    Catalogue embeds the exact retained five-source 15.x semantic corpus, stable identities, formula/operator index and
    machine-lineage law/build/migration records. External predecessor files are no longer required for current meaning.
    Structured v15.10 owners remain the new abstract design; retained payload supplies compatibility meaning only where
    no explicit current supersession exists. Derivative graph edges/index slices are regenerated and do not become
    parallel semantic owners.

END OF GARDEN VERSION HISTORY THROUGH v15.10
